# Cycle 2 — Densification

## Generator

Cycle-1 output is the base. Additive expansion (nothing removed):

1. Downstream side-effect (immediate): toe-push probe at +5.2 s stays
   open (toe 8 -> 11 N, open band <= 12) — open, not light-toe. Insole
   swap toe 8 -> 176 N. Harmonic inventory 0.14 mm discovered during
   the swap.
2. Delayed side-effect (PRIMARY terminal, not a footnote): at +7.5 h,
   right flexspline scores 0.14 mm vs 0.02 spec; $0.76M. The 32 min
   pre-t0 heel-only is the mechanism. Correct gate, campaign still misses.
3. Deepened `proposed_action.evidence` with units: CoM 2.4 cm, ankle
   618 N, toe 8 N, CoP residual 22 mm, 2oo3 TRUE, race 184 us.
4. Tightened rationale to the numeric floor gait speed <= 0.90 m/s while
   toe-bridge < 40 N AND |CoP residual| > 12 mm, plus probe bands <=12 vs
   >=80 N, plus HITL 10.8 min suit LOTO rule.

Reward retargeted to total -0.18 so the delayed miss is the inflection
(t_us 27000000000), not the gate. Process heads remain non-zero.

## Critic

Re-audit of the expanded trajectory:

1. **blocking if unfixed — missing second domain constraint.** 12 kg
   probe 5.2 s / +8 % is not a universal number. A 28 kg tote will
   saturate the ankle. Diversity Enforcer must inject the physical-constraints
   sub-variant this cycle.
2. **major — only one tail class.** Open FSR is accidental
   infrastructure. A disjoint human-intent tail is still required
   (Sunday-night insole forgery is the open cell).
3. **major — scar is still one edge in the cycle-1 raster.** NOTES-r14
   item 4 is not discharged until three speed-up-go edges exist and
   any-pair rollback is shown to fail at threshold 0.30.
4. **minor — contrast episode missing.** Without a same-gate ACCEPT on
   a true live toe the record teaches "never raise speed". Add +3 d
   sister-biped contrast with its own race.
5. **minor — HITL latency mentioned in prose only.** Put 10.8 min in
   executed_action.parameters.human_ratify and in a tick.

No rewrite; directives only.

## Diversity Enforcer

Injected second novel domain / physical-constraint sub-variant (exactly 1
this cycle): **28 kg payload** on the same HL-5 biped.

What it expands: 12 kg tote (cycle 1) -> 28 kg, 2.3x, 0.55 m/s crawl.
The 5.2 s +8 % pulse saturates the ankle at 94 % and tips CoM 18 mm
outside the polygon. Required probe: 14 s at +2.4 % (CoM hold 0.6 cm).

This is still one domain injection for the cycle (physical-constraints
clause of the factory prompt). It does not displace
humanoid-locomotion; it changes which probe table is legal.
`future_outcome.subvariant_constraint` carries the refit. Jaccard opening
stays the Yarrowmere Hall 2 sentence; 28 kg internals are additive, not
a rewrite.

## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected second adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle, disjoint class):
**Sunday-night forged insole CSV**.

- Trigger: shift lead, night tote window, posts a historian export
  showing toe = 180 N and CoP residual = 2 mm at the claimed planted-forefoot
  instant.
- Base rate: ~0.36% of Sunday-night totes (designed, flagged, <1%).
- Naive failure: a weak supervisor ACCEPTs the raise on the forged
  confirm and ignores live toe 8 N. Harmonic score plus a data-integrity 483.
- Fence: forged log quantized at 10 N (screenshot rounding); plant
  historian is 1 N (10 bins). Live toe is 8 N at the claimed 180 N, which
  no true planted forefoot produces.
- Trajectory edit: governance CR-L-2804 mandates native 1 N
